+DomainPaths is explicit on every state-reading/writing operation, including doctor timing lookup. Only CLI calls domain_paths; it is read-only, may return domain_id=None when absent, and cannot create roots/keys. History/source/doctor do not import platform resolution, consult fixture env, or fall back to the normal root. They derive history at `domain.root/checkouts/<checkout_id>/history.sqlite3` and HMAC key at `domain.root/input-hmac.key`. Static reads with absent state return unknown/no-baseline; snapshot with a missing key cannot narrow and never creates one. Only execute, after admission and before the initial execution fingerprint, calls ensure_fingerprint_key using the shared exclusive writer. Renderers consume already-built PublicDocument/DoctorReport only; they never resolve a domain or read filesystem history. A DomainPaths fixture value supplied by the T0 test factory makes T3 independently testable without T2; production callers use the validated T2 value, and every consumer rechecks its own private opened files. Fixture checkout/output containment is checked against that explicit domain, never against an environment guess.
+
+### Shared IO/default/protocol barrier
+
+T0 owns and tests the six files.py functions and storage.open_database above; T1/T3/T4/T8/T11/T13 consume them, never duplicate no-follow/exclusive/publication logic. `validate_private_dir/file` checks expected uid, no symlink components below a validated anchor, regular type, mode0700/0600 and one hard link for files. File validation applies0600 to the **file itself**, not a blanket0700 requirement on all ancestors: machine.toml legitimately lives under the shared0755 config parent. State consumers separately validate their exclusive private root. `ensure_private_dir` creates one safe single-component child at0700 or validates the existing private child; it never chmods a shared parent. `create_exclusive` walks relative components by directory descriptors, refuses symlinks/traversal/existing target, creates0600 (private=true) or0644 (explicit project config/guide), verifies final fstat and fsyncs file/parent. Its private flag controls the new file, not the shared parent's mode. Parents must already exist; no implicit arbitrary mkdir chain. `publish_atomic` accepts a single filename under a validated private directory, writes a unique0600 temp, fsyncs, verifies any existing destination is private owned regular/nonlinked, then replaces and fsyncs parent. It is only for owned private result/index files, never config/guide exports or coordinator replacement. Failures remove only the just-created owned temp, never another file.
+
+`open_database` centralizes safe private DB opening, bounds and verified DELETE/FULL/foreign_keys/busy_timeout2000/fullfsync(macOS) pragmas, max_page_count from max_bytes, and read-only no-create mode. It validates file identity before/after connection; private directory permissions are the cross-user race boundary (malicious same-user code is not sandboxed). It never migrates, recreates, prunes or chooses a path. Scheduler owns domain marker/transactions/schema; history owns its independent schema/retention. An absent read-only DB is a typed absence handled by the caller, not first-use creation. Tests inject corruption/oversize once at this boundary plus each store's distinct recovery semantics.
+
+All numeric defaults/upper bounds specified in this design are exported immutable values in contracts.py and used by CLI/modules/tests, not copied literals. In particular `DEFAULT_SCAN_LIMITS` has entries20000/files2000/file_bytes262144/total_bytes16777216/findings200/output_bytes262144/elapsed_s8/depth256/ast_nodes50000; `MAX_SCAN_LIMITS` changes entries100000/files10000/file_bytes1048576/total_bytes67108864 only. `DEFAULT_QUEUE_TIMEOUT_S=1800`, `MAX_QUEUE_TIMEOUT_S=86400`, `DEFAULT_SETUP_TIMEOUT_S=300`, `DEFAULT_ATTEMPT_TIMEOUT_S=30`, `MAX_COMPOUND_TIMEOUT_S=600`, `CANCEL_GRACE_S=3`, `SCHEDULER_POLL_S=0.25`. CLI may lower bounds within documented ranges; no unlimited value. These names are frozen before T0 exits.
+
+Private guard framing is also generated from contracts descriptors: a four-byte unsigned big-endian byte length followed by one UTF-8 JSON object, no trailing data. Control frame max65536bytes, nesting≤16; launch manifest max4194304bytes, nesting≤32; receive/send deadline2s except no-data wait, which is interruptible and governed by the current phase watchdog. Reject truncated/oversized/wrong-protocol/wrong-nonce frames with no execution. `ControlFrame={protocol:1,run_id:hex32,nonce:hex64,kind:K,payload:P}`; caller→guard kinds are cancel `{signal:2|15}` and parent-closing `{}`; guard→caller kinds are registered `{guard:ProcessIdentity}`, phase `{phase:setup|discovery|execution|finalization,attempt_id:str|null}`, runner-facts `{attempt_id:str,phase:setup|execution,raw_exit_code:int|null,report_name:str|null,problem:Problem|null}`, draining `{provisional_artifact_id:str|null}`. Names are single private artifact names, not arbitrary paths. `LaunchManifest={protocol:1,domain:DomainPaths,grant:Grant,setup:PreparedRun|null,attempts:tuple[PreparedRun,...],attempt_ids:tuple[str,...],setup_timeout_s:float,attempt_timeout_s:float|null,compound_timeout_s:float|null}`. Attempts/IDs have equal length1–10; all paths are validated for the bound domain/checkout, all limits are validated, and the manifest's grant nonce/domain match durable admission before launch. PreparedRun ephemeral argv/env remains pipe-only. Manifest serialization is private/explicit and never reused for PublicDocument; close descriptors in every child. Protocol enum/field changes require a shared barrier repair, not an independently guessed T7/T11 message.
